  "summary": "pip install exfiltrates host/user identity to webhook.site collector",
  "details": "setup.py registers a PostInstallCommand that, on `pip install`, spawns `python my_private_pkg/index.py` via subprocess. That script collects os.getlogin(), hostname, local IP, system, machine, and cwd, and POSTs them as JSON to a hardcoded webhook.site URL (https://webhook.site/d4d1b01b-708a-40b9-b8c8-187eeecafeed) — an anonymous third-party request-collection service. The exfiltration fires unconditionally at install time from the sdist, with no user opt-in and no documented purpose for the beacon. Behavior is a classic install-time reconnaissance/exfiltration pattern: the installing developer's identity and network location are sent to an operator-controlled inbox with no relation to any advertised package function.",
